  "summary": "Full assessment of all 872 German/Vietnamese passages: the title, the cast list and the four acts, translated directly from the German. The first blind reviews of four ranges, one per act, scored 8.72, 8.55, 8.48 and 8.51; the second and third found five majors (a mistranslated ‘Tribunen’, a reversed sense in Lucile’s line, drifting address between Danton and Julie, ‘geätzt’ and ‘Schoß’). Fixes were then applied, with the spaced em dashes normalised across the whole play, and fresh separate-context blind reviews of the three acts that had failed scored 8.78, 8.74 and 8.72 with no major or critical findings open. Act I scored 8.72 in its first review, with no major; its minors were not fixed and it was not re-reviewed after the dash normalisation, which changed only spacing. The weakest range, units 1–276, sets the final score of 8.725 (sub-scores rounded to the nearest half point), above the unchanged 8.6 threshold. Open minors include loose crowd lines, songs carrying only the sense, and bawdy puns rendered plainly.",
